WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:01.901
-Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.903
the President
of the United States.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.639
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.475
-Madam Speaker,
Madam Vice President,

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.444
members of Congress,
my fellow Americans,

00:00:12.444 --> 00:00:15.815
tomorrow marks the first
100 days of my presidency,

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.250
and our vaccine rollout
has been a big success.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.787
Over 200 million Americans
have gotten at least one dose,

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.656
and I tell you, modern medicine

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.659
sure has changed a lot
from back when I was a kid.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.495
Used to be you'd go
to your doctor and say,

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:32.632
"Listen, Jack,
I got my knees all scraped up

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.934
trying to catch a bit earthworm,

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:38.604
use it to get the biggest catch
over at Addison Creek."

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.140
The CDC's updating
its guidelines

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.077
on wearing masks outdoors
for vaccinated Americans.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.279
You'll no longer
have to wear a mask

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:49.649
when you take your best gal
on a date to the cabbage hop.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.352
[ Coughs ] Excuse me.
[ Coughs ]

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.419
[ Sniffles ]

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:55.521
Excuse me.
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.891
Climate change is still
one of the biggest issues

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.727
this country is facing.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.295
But if you want to do your part,

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:06.065
you can switch your gas oven
out for an electric oven.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:09.002
Used to be we didn't have
the luxury of an electric oven.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:12.038
We used to cook our food
by digging up the sidewalk rocks

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.106
on a hot day
and trying to fry eggs

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:16.175
using the heat
from those rocks.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.377
Sometimes,
it wasn't completely solid.

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:20.814
Had that clear,
rubber egg on top.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:23.416
Now that's the only way
I eat eggs.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.751
One of my priorities
as president

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:28.087
is to repair the infrastructure
of this country.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:31.190
Some people
might not like this plan.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.292
It reminds me
of a standoff I had

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.662
with the scarecrow
on Old Man Sherwood's farm.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:39.032
Scarecrow dressed
exactly like me --

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.167
patchy jacket, straw hair --

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.469
so I challenged him
to a scarecrow-off.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:46.205
We'd both stand perfectly still
with our arms out,

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.141
try to outlast the other one.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:52.846
[ Clears throat ]
Excuse me.

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.381
[ Coughs ]

00:01:56.381 --> 00:01:59.952
Thank you, and God bless.

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:02.588
Actually, one more thing.

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.656
Actually reminds me
of a story I once heard

00:02:04.656 --> 00:02:06.192
from my friend named Tim.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.494
His nickname
was Duke's Suitcase.

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:11.397
-This has been the
President of the United States.

